      "body": "Help with transporter authorisation Your transporter must hold a valid transporter authorisation, issued by DAERA or APHA in the UK if they are: transporting any live vertebrate animals in, to, from or through Great Britain (GB) travelling on journeys of over 65 km transporting as part of an economic (commercial) activity Find out how to transport animals in connection with an economic activity (opens in a new tab) Documents issued by DAERA are valid for use in GB. Documents issued in any EU member state are not valid for use in GB."
